2026-11-13T10:02:15.7216173Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7226336Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7227517Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7228206Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7228427Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7228776Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7229169Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7229461Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7229915Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7230259Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7230415Z If you would like to
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7230782Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7230988Z 
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7231306Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7231830Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-13T10:02:15.7232068Z 
